      "title": "Pentagon official and former Aukus sceptic says deal is ‘full steam ahead’, echoing Trump",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/13/pentagon-official-and-former-aukus-sceptic-says-deal-is-full-steam-ahead-echoing-trump",
      "description": "<p>Elbridge Colby, a US under secretary of war, says he is ‘very pleased’ with the nuclear submarine program’s progress</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Elbridge Colby, the third-highest-ranking official at the Pentagon and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jun/12/australian-government-downplays-natural-decision-by-pentagon-to-review-aukus-defence-pact\">formerly an avowed Aukus sceptic</a>, has mirrored his president’s language on the nuclear submarine deal, saying it is “full steam ahead”.</p><p>Colby, a US under secretary of war, was the author of the Trump administration’s review of the Aukus deal, which would see the US sell three in-service Virginia-class submarines to Australia, before the development of Australia’s domestically built Aukus-class submarines.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/13/pentagon-official-and-former-aukus-sceptic-says-deal-is-full-steam-ahead-echoing-trump\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T08:20:43"
    },
